,"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/incidentEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/incidentEdges(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/neighbors(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/oppositeVertex(to:acrossEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/vertex(atIndex:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/vertexIndex(of:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedView"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges and their identity.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" lists every edge once (each copy of a parallel edge, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each self-loop, once), and an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" is its identity. The edge is reached","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from both its endpoints through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of:)"},{"text":", always at that one position, so a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keyed by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"text":" (a weight) is the same in both directions. Positions are valid until the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is mutated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Neighborhoods count edge ends. A vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w ≠ v"},{"type":"text","text":" appears in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once per edge between them. A self-loop has both its ends at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" appears in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" twice per loop, and the loop’s position twice in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacency_list"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON, igraph). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of either, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop counts 2 and the degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex and edge indices."}]},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives adjacency in index space. A representation with dense edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices also reports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps edge positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_index"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":"), so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them parallel to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every conformer satisfies:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"vertexCount == vertices.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices; ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount == edges.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" as an endpoint;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oppositeVertex(to: v, acrossEdgeAt: e)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e].oppositeVertex(to: v)"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the opposite vertices in the same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", in either orientation, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains"},{"type":"text","text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Asking again gives the same answer.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" is in index order: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atIndex: i)"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":"th vertex.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapped through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"text":", in the same order.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[e]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ends mapped through ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With edge indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound == edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is one-to-one onto"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and, with vertex indices too,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" mapped through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With edge indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index order: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"th position of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":". So an algorithm that gathers edges from the index-space rows can order them by position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a tie rule) without walking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Defaults.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" As for ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", members with default implementations are requirements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a representation’s faster version is the one generic code calls, and a wrapper must forward","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has no mutation; mutation belongs to concrete types. It does not refine","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/Graph.swift#L56","fileName":"Graph.swift"},"fragments":[{"te